WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.263
Millions of people visit the Louvre Museum in Paris each year.

2
00:00:05.264 --> 00:00:10.640
Many want a glimpse of one painting in particular—the Mona Lisa

3
00:00:10.641 --> 00:00:15.295
. The Louvre is its home now, but the painting has moved around a

4
00:00:15.296 --> 00:00:19.641
lot. Leonardo da Vinci began working on the portrait in

5
00:00:19.642 --> 00:00:25.123
Italy. He started it sometime between 1503 and

6
00:00:25.124 --> 00:00:30.565
1506. In 1516 the French king invited da Vinci to

7
00:00:30.566 --> 00:00:36.451
France. Da Vinci accepted, and he brought the painting with him when he

8
00:00:36.452 --> 00:00:40.902
moved. Before da Vinci died, the French king bought the

9
00:00:40.903 --> 00:00:47.689
painting. Later French kings hung it in their palaces until

10
00:00:47.690 --> 00:00:53.013
1793. That year the Louvre Palace became a public

11
00:00:53.014 --> 00:00:57.686
museum. The Mona Lisa was put on display in the

12
00:00:57.687 --> 00:01:00.132
museum. But it did not stay there for

13
00:01:00.133 --> 00:01:06.261
long. Within a decade, Napoleon took over France, and the Mona Lisa moved

14
00:01:06.262 --> 00:01:10.764
again. Napoleon hung the painting in his own

15
00:01:10.765 --> 00:01:14.748
bedroom! Soon it ended up back on display in the

16
00:01:14.749 --> 00:01:18.665
Louvre. The Mona Lisa was not a very popular painting

17
00:01:18.666 --> 00:01:24.064
though. This all changed in August

18
00:01:24.065 --> 00:01:30.179
1911. On a Tuesday morning, a visitor to the museum noticed the painting was

19
00:01:30.180 --> 00:01:33.043
gone. At first the museum staff didn't

20
00:01:33.044 --> 00:01:40.292
worry. Paintings were often removed to be cleaned or

21
00:01:40.293 --> 00:01:46.736
photographed. But soon the staff realized something was terribly

22
00:01:46.737 --> 00:01:49.882
wrong. The painting had been

23
00:01:49.883 --> 00:01:55.061
stolen! It turned out that an Italian man named Vincenzo Peruggia had taken

24
00:01:55.062 --> 00:02:00.764
it. He believed that the Italian masterpiece belonged in Italy, not France.

25
00:02:00.765 --> 00:02:07.054
So Peruggia, a handyman for the museum, came up with a plan.

26
00:02:07.055 --> 00:02:11.088
He knew the museum was always closed on Mondays.

27
00:02:11.089 --> 00:02:16.689
One Sunday, after the museum closed for the day, he hid in a closet.

28
00:02:16.690 --> 00:02:20.209
The next morning, he removed the frame from the painting.

29
00:02:20.210 --> 00:02:23.611
He hid the Mona Lisa under his jacket.

30
00:02:23.612 --> 00:02:27.032
Then he walked right out of the museum!

31
00:02:27.033 --> 00:02:30.771
The bold theft made headlines around the world.

32
00:02:30.772 --> 00:02:35.937
Instantly the Mona Lisa became the world's most famous painting.

33
00:02:35.938 --> 00:02:40.645
For two years Peruggia kept the painting hidden in a trunk.

34
00:02:40.646 --> 00:02:43.901
Eventually he returned to Italy.

35
00:02:43.902 --> 00:02:50.119
He tried to sell the painting there and was caught.

36
00:02:50.120 --> 00:02:53.749
The painting returned to the Louvre more famous than ever.

37
00:02:53.750 --> 00:02:57.132
It has moved around several more times since then.

38
00:02:57.133 --> 00:03:01.554
During World War II, it was hidden for protection.

39
00:03:01.555 --> 00:03:05.896
Later it traveled to other famous museums around the world.

40
00:03:05.897 --> 00:03:10.383
But mostly the painting has stayed in the Louvre.

41
00:03:10.384 --> 00:03:13.470
The Mona Lisa gets lots of attention.

42
00:03:13.471 --> 00:03:16.491
But not all of that attention is good.

43
00:03:16.492 --> 00:03:21.809
Over the years several people have tried to damage the painting.

44
00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:27.289
So guards stand nearby, and a wooden rail keeps crowds a safe distance away.

45
00:03:27.290 --> 00:03:31.538
The painting also has a glass case that protects and preserves it.

46
00:03:31.539 --> 00:03:35.597
The Mona Lisa might be on the move again in the future.

47
00:03:35.598 --> 00:03:38.908
But the Louvre is its permanent home.

48
00:03:38.909 --> 00:03:44.966
If you ever want to see it, you know exactly where to go!

